  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Exact retained way/27859115 and Q2595999 identify Saint Nicholas in Prague Old Town,not the other Prague Saint Nicholas church. Current standard viewer whole35184399947947 and six tower/dome/lantern parts35184834500034–39 retain83 raw outline points and all properties,with the earlier whole/multilingual tags and same-ID Saint Nicholas POI. Anchor[14.419905274,50.08790284] and heading0.190715332884rad unchanged;no horizontal rescale. Native+X east rounded apse,−X west secondary portal,+Z south ornate twin-tower frontage/Old Town Square. Named square and south-front/east-apse pictures resolve the undirected axis;facing approximate3°. Neighboring houses to north/west and the southwest square-edge buildings remain host content.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Current map whole height18m;two lower tower parts28m,two upper crown/lantern parts36m,central octagonal drum/dome part32m,and central lantern part41m. These tags are retained as nominal whole/component controls,not surveyed dimensions or proof of exact roof datum. Above floor0.5m:body cornice18m,tile roof22.6m;lower tower wall28m,green lower helmet30.7m,open upper lantern30.7–34.1m and upper bulb36m;thin spire/finial tips40.8m are picture estimates beyond the upper-part tag. Central drum25.5m/copper bell roof32m,white lantern37.2m and copper cap/finial41m. Facade crown23.2m,portals/steps,window/bay partitions,apse roof22.5m,decorative figures/crest/capital/scroll profiles are estimates. No independent height facts."
  },
